:"2025-08-18T13:57:32Z","closed_at":"2025-08-18T13:56:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.5 beta5\n\n### System information\n\nMac OS Sequoia 15.6\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen exporting to Android (Both Gradle and non) the editor looks for a non existant file outputting this error.\n\nOutput with Gradle:\n```\n  ERROR: Can't open file from path ''.\n  ERROR: Cannot create file 'res://android/build/assets/'.\n```\n**This breaks the gradle build as the export doesn't include any assets**\n\nNormal export instead prints only \n`  ERROR: Can't open file from path ''.`\nAnd the built apk still works\n\nDeleting everything (but the imported dir) from the .godot folders fixes the issues for a while. I can't tell exactly when it starts doing it again, but it does shortly after I get to work on the project again.\n\nI could reproduce this only on a big project with 8gb of assets so I don't exclude the cause is one of them. In that case I'd like some help on how to find out which one it is. Still, the gradle build shouldn't fail for a missing file\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open a project\n- Export to Android\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nI couldn't reproduce this on a minimal project","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://ap